#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:69
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "はじめに"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:71
msgid ""
"In this exercise, we will perform metadynamics [1] and path-metadynamics "
"(PMD) [2-4] simulations of a system that can undergo a transition between "
"two free energy minima. These two stable states are separated by a "
"transition state barrier, so that the transition process is a _rare event_ "
"for ``normal'' (i.e. unbiased) molecular dynamics simulations."
msgstr ""
"この演習では、2つの自由エネルギー極小の間を遷移する系の Metadynamics [1] と Path-metadynamics (PMD) "
"[2-4] を実行します。2つの安定状態は Transition State の Barrier で隔てられているため、「通常の」、すなわち Bias "
"のない Molecular Dynamics では、この遷移は _Rare Event_ になります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:78
msgid ""
"PMD is able to simultaneously and efficiently converge the transition path "
"(which can be either an average transition path or a minimum free energy "
"path (MFEP)) and the free energy profile of the process along this path. "
"This is achieved by performing metadynamics on an adaptive path connecting "
"the two known stable states."
msgstr ""
"PMD は Transition Path（Average Transition Path または Minimum Free Energy Path "
"(MFEP)）と、その Path に沿う自由エネルギープロファイルを同時かつ効率的に収束させられます。既知の2つの安定状態を結ぶ Adaptive "
"Path 上で Metadynamics を行うことで実現します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:84
msgid ""
"In order to understand the principles and advantages of PMD, we will first "
"perform standard metadynamics and get familiar with its parameters and "
"functionalities. Subsequently, we will add the features corresponding to the"
" adaptive path. To ease computation and visualization, we will employ a "
"simple model system."
msgstr ""
"PMD の原理と利点を理解するため、まず標準的な Metadynamics を実行し、そのパラメータと機能に慣れます。その後、Adaptive Path"
" に対応する機能を追加します。計算と可視化を容易にするため、簡単なモデル系を使います。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:90
msgid ""
"This exercise makes use of PLUMED's [5] own internal engine: _plumed pesmd_,"
" i.e. without being coupled to an MD engine that runs an actual molecular "
"system. The advantages are that the simulations will be very fast, and you "
"do not need to know anything about the MD engine of our choice, which might "
"be different from the one that you are used to."
msgstr ""
"この演習では PLUMED [5] 内蔵のエンジン _plumed pesmd_ を使い、実際の分子系を扱う MD "
"エンジンとは結合しません。シミュレーションが非常に高速で、普段とは異なるかもしれない MD エンジンの使い方を学ぶ必要がないという利点があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:96
msgid ""
"Still, the enhanced sampling techniques that you will use in this exercise, "
"and the plumed input files that we will write for that, can also be used "
"(with very little changes) with plumed patched to any MD software, which "
"means that you can potentially use it for your own research!"
msgstr ""
"ここで使う Enhanced Sampling 法と作成する plumed 入力ファイルは、ごくわずかな変更で、任意の MD ソフトウェアに Patch"
" した plumed でも使えます。自分の研究にも応用できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:102
msgid ""
"In order to overcome the timescale limitations of MD and be able to observe "
"relevant molecular transitions, the community has developed a plethora of "
"enhanced sampling methods. Among them, we can identify the so-called biasing"
" methods, which work by exerting an external potential (or force) on a few "
"key descriptive degrees of freedom of the transition, commonly called "
"_collective variables_ (CVs)."
msgstr ""
"MD の時間スケールの制約を克服して重要な分子遷移を観測するため、多くの Enhanced Sampling 法が開発されてきました。その中に "
"Biasing 法があります。遷移を記述する少数の重要な自由度、一般に _Collective Variables_ (CVs) と呼ばれる変数に、外部"
" Potential または力を加える方法です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:110
msgid ""
"The choice and design of CVs is a task of great importance. In the "
"following, we will assume that the CVs are known. We will consider a "
"molecular system whose free energy surface (FES) is fully described by a set"
" of $N$ CVs, $\\{z_i(\\mathbf{q}\\,)\\}$ with $i=1... N$, which are all "
"functions of the system's particle positions $\\mathbf{q}(t)$. We will also "
"assume that these particle positions $\\mathbf{q}(t)$ evolve in time with a "
"canonical equilibrium distribution at temperature $T$ under a potential "
"$V(\\mathbf{q})$."
msgstr ""
"CV の選択と設計は非常に重要です。以下では CV は既知とします。自由エネルギー表面 (FES) が $N$ 個の "
"CV、$\\{z_i(\\mathbf{q}\\,)\\}$、$i=1... N$ で完全に記述される分子系を考えます。これらはすべて粒子位置 "
"$\\mathbf{q}(t)$ の関数です。また、粒子位置 $\\mathbf{q}(t)$ は Potential $V(\\mathbf{q})$"
" の下で、温度 $T$ の Canonical 平衡分布に従って時間発展すると仮定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:120
msgid "Metadynamics"
msgstr "Metadynamics"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:122
msgid ""
"We are interested in exploring the space spanned by the CVs, $\\{z_i\\}$, "
"and in quantifying the free energy. In order to do so, in metadynamics we "
"exert a history-dependent repulsive potential by summing Gaussian kernels "
"over time:"
msgstr ""
"CV $\\{z_i\\}$ が張る空間を探索し、自由エネルギーを定量化することが目的です。Metadynamics では、時間とともに "
"Gaussian Kernel を足し合わせ、履歴に依存する反発 Potential を加えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:132
msgid ""
"with Gaussian height $H$, widths along each CV $W_i$, and depositing "
"frequency $\\tau$. This bias drives the system away from already visited "
"configurations and into new regions of CV-space. More importantly, in the "
"long-time limit, the bias potential converges to the minus free energy as "
"function of the CVs: $V_\\text{bias}(\\mathbf{z},t \\rightarrow \\infty) = -"
" F(\\mathbf{z})$."
msgstr ""
"ここで Gaussian の高さは $H$、各 CV に沿う幅は $W_i$、追加間隔は $\\tau$ です。この Bias により、既に訪れた "
"Configuration から離れ、CV 空間の新しい領域へ移動します。さらに、長時間極限で BiasPotential は CV "
"の関数としての自由エネルギーの符号を反転したものに収束します：$V_\\text{bias}(\\mathbf{z},t \\rightarrow "
"\\infty) = - F(\\mathbf{z})$。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:139
msgid ""
"As a well-established sampling technique, metadynamics also has several "
"extensions to accelerate convergence and improve computational performance, "
"such as the multiple-walker and well-tempered versions [6,7]."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics は確立された Sampling 法であり、収束や計算性能を改善する Multiple-walker 版、Well-"
"tempered 版などの拡張があります [6,7]。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:143
msgid ""
"Metadynamics can handle a few CVs simultaneously in a trivial manner, which "
"spares us from having to find a single perfect CV. Instead, an appropriate "
"set of CVs allows us to converge an insightful multidimensional free energy "
"landscape, in which (meta)stable states and connecting MFEPs can be "
"identified. In practice however, especially when investigating complex "
"transitions, the number of CVs is limited to $N\\approx3$, because of the "
"exponential growth of computational cost with CV dimensionality."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics は少数の CV を容易に同時に扱えるため、完璧な単一の CV を見つける必要がありません。適切な CV "
"の組を使えば、多次元の自由エネルギー地形を収束させ、安定・準安定状態と、それらを結ぶ MFEP を特定できます。ただし実際には、特に複雑な遷移では、CV"
" の次元とともに計算コストが指数関数的に増えるため、CV 数は $N\\approx3$ に制限されます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:152
msgid "Path-metadynamics"
msgstr "Path-metadynamics"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:154
msgid ""
"In order to tackle complex transitions that require many CVs, path-based "
"methods were developed. In these schemes, a path-CV is introduced. That is, "
"a parametrized curve that connects two FES basins --- the known stable "
"states $A$ and $B$ --- in the space spanned by the CVs: "
"$\\mathbf{s}(\\sigma): \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^N$, where the "
"parameter $\\sigma(\\mathbf{z}\\,) | _{s} : \\mathbb{R}^N \\rightarrow "
"[0,1]$ yields the progress along the path from $A$ to $B$, such that "
"$\\mathbf{s}(0) \\in A$ and $\\mathbf{s}(1) \\in B$."
msgstr ""
"多数の CV が必要な複雑な遷移を扱うため、Path に基づく方法が開発されました。これらでは Path-CV、すなわち CV が張る空間で2つの "
"FES Basin（既知の安定状態 $A$ と $B$）を結ぶパラメータ付き曲線 $\\mathbf{s}(\\sigma): \\mathbb{R} "
"\\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^N$ を導入します。パラメータ $\\sigma(\\mathbf{z}\\,) | _{s} : "
"\\mathbb{R}^N \\rightarrow [0,1]$ は、$\\mathbf{s}(0) \\in A$、$\\mathbf{s}(1) "
"\\in B$ となるよう、$A$ から $B$ への Path に沿う進行度を表します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:164
msgid ""
"This progress parameter emulates the reaction coordinate and can in "
"principle be connected to the committor value. Since the transition path "
"curve is not known a priori, the path-CV must be adaptive. If we assume "
"that, in the vicinity of the path, the iso-commitor planes $S_\\sigma$ are "
"perpendicular to $\\mathbf{s}(\\sigma)$, and that the configurational "
"probability is a good indicator of the transition flux density, then we can "
"converge the average transition path by iteratively adapting a guess path to"
" the cumulative average density: $\\mathbf{s}_g(\\sigma_g) = "
"\\langle\\mathbf{z}\\,\\rangle _{\\sigma_g}$ [3]."
msgstr ""
"この進行度パラメータは Reaction Coordinate を模倣し、原理的には Committor 値と関連付けられます。Transition "
"Path の曲線は事前にわからないため、Path-CV は Adaptive である必要があります。Path 近傍で Iso-committor 平面 "
"$S_\\sigma$ が $\\mathbf{s}(\\sigma)$ に垂直であり、Configuration の確率が遷移 Flux "
"密度のよい指標になると仮定すれば、推定 Path を累積平均密度 $\\mathbf{s}_g(\\sigma_g) = "
"\\langle\\mathbf{z}\\,\\rangle _{\\sigma_g}$ に反復的に適応させることで Average "
"Transition Path を収束させられます [3]。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:175
msgid ""
"The key advantage of PMD is that the metadynamics biasing can be performed "
"on the 1D progress parameter along the adaptive path-CV, instead of the "
"$N$-dimensional CV-space. PMD is able to converge a path, and the free "
"energy along it, with a sublinear rise in computational cost with respect to"
" the growth in CV dimensionality (instead of the exponential relation when "
"not using a path-CV)[4]."
msgstr ""
"PMD の主な利点は、$N$ 次元 CV 空間の代わりに、Adaptive Path-CV に沿う1次元の進行度パラメータに Metadynamics "
"の Bias を加えられることです。PMD では、CV 次元の増加に対する計算コストの増加が線形未満でも、Path "
"とそれに沿う自由エネルギーを収束させられます。Path-CV を使わない場合は指数関数的に増加します [4]。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:182
msgid ""
"Numerically, the adaptive path-CV is implemented as a set of $M$ ordered "
"nodes (coordinates in CV-space) $\\mathbf{s}_g (\\sigma_g,t) \\rightarrow "
"{\\mathbf{s}^{\\,t_i}_j}$ with $j=1,...,M$, where $t_i$ is the discrete time"
" of path updates. The projection of any point $\\mathbf{z}$ onto the path is"
" done considering the closest two nodes, and $\\sigma$ is obtained by "
"interpolation. This approach requires equidistant nodes, which are imposed "
"by a reparametrization step after each path update. The update step for the "
"path nodes is done by:"
msgstr ""
"数値的には、Adaptive Path-CV は順序を持つ $M$ 個の Node（CV 空間の座標）の集合 $\\mathbf{s}_g "
"(\\sigma_g,t) \\rightarrow {\\mathbf{s}^{\\,t_i}_j}$、$j=1,...,M$ "
"として実装されます。$t_i$ は Path 更新の離散時刻です。任意の点 $\\mathbf{z}$ の Path への射影には最も近い2つの "
"Node を使い、補間で $\\sigma$ を得ます。この方法では等間隔の Node が必要なため、各 Path 更新後に "
"Reparametrization を行います。Path の Node は次の式で更新します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:198
msgid ""
"where $k$ is the current MD step and $w$ is the weight of the adjustment, "
"which is non-zero only for the two nodes closest to the average CV density. "
"We also introduce the fade factor $\\xi =\\exp( -\\ln(2) / \\tau_{1/2})$, "
"with $\\tau_{1/2}$ as a half-life: the number of MD steps after which the "
"distances measured from the path weight only 50 % of its original value. A "
"short half-life increases path flexibility by allowing it to rapidly "
"``forget'' a bad initial guess, while a long half-life restricts the path "
"fluctuations and leads eventually to optimal convergence. The first and last"
" nodes, located at the stable states $A$ and $B$ respectively, remain fixed."
" Extra trailing nodes can be placed at both ends of the path to better "
"capture the free energy valleys. Wall potentials can be used to keep the "
"sampling near the relevant [0,1] $\\sigma$-interval."
msgstr ""
"ここで $k$ は現在の MD Step、$w$ は調整の重みであり、平均 CV 密度に最も近い2つの Node 以外では0です。また Fade "
"Factor $\\xi =\\exp( -\\ln(2) / \\tau_{1/2})$ を導入します。$\\tau_{1/2}$ "
"は半減期で、Path から測った距離の重みが元の50%になるまでの MD Step 数です。短い半減期では不適切な初期推定を速やかに「忘れる」ため "
"Path が柔軟になり、長い半減期では Path の揺らぎが抑えられ、最終的に最適な収束に達します。安定状態 $A$、$B$ にある最初と最後の "
"Node は固定します。自由エネルギーの谷をよりよく捉えるため、Path の両端に Trailing Node を追加できます。Wall "
"Potential を使えば、対象の [0,1] $\\sigma$ 区間の近くで Sampling を維持できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:212
msgid ""
"Additionally, a harmonic restraint set on $|| \\mathbf{z}_k - "
"\\mathbf{s}^{\\,t_{i}} ( \\sigma (\\mathbf{z}_k) ) ||$ can help in "
"converging to a specific transition path in scenarios with multiple or ill-"
"defined transition channels. We refer to this restraint as a ``tube'' "
"potential. In the limit of an infinitesimally narrow tube potential, the "
"path update step follows the local free energy gradient and PMD converges to"
" the MFEP instead of the average transition path. This control over the "
"behavior of the algorithm is an advantageous feature, as switching from a "
"density-driven to a gradient-driven path optimization leads either to the "
"average transition path or the MFEP."
msgstr ""
"さらに、$|| \\mathbf{z}_k - \\mathbf{s}^{\\,t_{i}} ( \\sigma (\\mathbf{z}_k) ) "
"||$ に Harmonic Restraint を加えると、複数または不明瞭な Transition Channel がある場合に特定の "
"Transition Path へ収束させやすくなります。この Restraint を「Tube」Potential と呼びます。無限に細い Tube "
"Potential の極限では、Path の更新は局所的な自由エネルギー勾配に従い、PMD は Average Transition Path ではなく"
" MFEP に収束します。このようにアルゴリズムの挙動を制御できる点は利点です。密度に基づく Path "
"最適化と勾配に基づく最適化を切り替えることで、Average Transition Path または MFEP を得られます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:223
msgid ""
"Metadynamics, the method of choice to sample the path-CV, drives the system "
"back and forth along the path, providing sufficient sampling of the CV "
"density to localize the transition path. At the same time, metadynamics "
"continuously self-corrects the free energy by overwriting the previously "
"deposited Gaussians with new ones. This leads to a converged free energy "
"along the localized path: $V_\\text{bias}(\\sigma,t \\rightarrow \\infty) = "
"-F(\\sigma)$. Most of the algorithmic extensions developed for metadynamics "
"(well-tempered, transition-tempered, multiple walkers, etc.) can be "
"straightforwardly combined with the adaptive path-CV. Moreover, other "
"biasing techniques (umbrella sampling, constrained MD, steered MD, etc.) can"
" also be used to sample along the path, or even in the direction "
"perpendicular to it."
msgstr ""
"Path-CV の Sampling に用いる Metadynamics は、系を Path に沿って往復させ、Transition Path "
"の位置を特定するのに十分な CV 密度の Sampling を行います。同時に、以前追加した Gaussian の上に新しい Gaussian "
"を重ねることで、自由エネルギーを継続的に自己修正します。その結果、特定された Path "
"に沿う自由エネルギーが収束します：$V_\\text{bias}(\\sigma,t \\rightarrow \\infty) = "
"-F(\\sigma)$。Metadynamics 向けの拡張（Well-tempered、Transition-tempered、Multiple "
"Walkers など）のほとんどは、Adaptive Path-CV と容易に組み合わせられます。また、Umbrella "
"Sampling、Constrained MD、Steered MD などの Biasing 法でも、Path に沿って、あるいは垂直方向に "
"Sampling できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:237
msgid "Model system"
msgstr "モデル系"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:239
msgid ""
"In this exercise, we will sample the well-known M&uuml;ller-Brown (MB) "
"potential energy surface (PES). You can find more about it in Ref. [8]. We "
"add harmonic walls to limit the sampling within the interesting region of "
"the PES."
msgstr ""
"この演習では、よく知られた M&uuml;ller-Brown (MB) Potential Energy Surface (PES) を "
"Sampling します。詳細は文献 [8] を参照してください。関心のある PES 領域内に Sampling を制限するため、Harmonic "
"Wall を加えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:244
msgid ""
"![The two-dimension M&uuml;ller-Brown potential showing two minima connected"
" by a curvy reaction channel](mullerbrown.png)"
msgstr ""
"![曲がった Reaction Channel で結ばれる2つの極小を持つ2次元 M&uuml;ller-Brown "
"Potential](mullerbrown.png)"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:246
msgid "Using PLUMED"
msgstr "PLUMED の使い方"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:248
msgid ""
"To install PLUMED, if you have not already done this above, go to the folder"
" `plumed` in the folder for this exercise. In the script `install`, change "
"the prefix to the installation folder of your choice, and then run the "
"script. If you have issues with the installation you can check: "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-doc/html/_installation.html>"
msgstr ""
"上記の手順でまだ PLUMED をインストールしていない場合は、演習フォルダ内の `plumed` に移動します。`install` スクリプトの "
"prefix を希望するインストール先に変更し、スクリプトを実行します。問題が起きた場合は "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-doc/html/_installation.html> "
"を確認してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:255
msgid ""
"To visualize the results of this exercise, plotting script examples are "
"provided for the [gnuplot](http://www.gnuplot.info) plotting software (see "
"the script files names starting with `plot_` or `anim_`). Make sure to "
"change the corresponding variables according to your choices of the "
"metadynamics and path-CV parameters. Of course, feel free to use other "
"plotting tools, for example pythons matplotlib."
msgstr ""
"結果の可視化用に [gnuplot](http://www.gnuplot.info) の描画スクリプト例があります（名前が `plot_` または "
"`anim_` で始まるファイル）。Metadynamics と Path-CV "
"のパラメータ設定に合わせて、対応する変数を変更してください。Python の matplotlib など、ほかの描画ツールも自由に使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:262
msgid ""
"To run the PLUMED pesmd on the MB PES, use the command `plumed pesmd < "
"path/to/input`. The `input` file is located in the `Exercise` folder. Review"
" the PLUMED pesmd documentation: <https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.4/user-"
"doc/html/pesmd.html>."
msgstr ""
"MB PES 上で PLUMED pesmd を実行するには、`plumed pesmd < path/to/input` を使います。`input` "
"は `Exercise` にあります。PLUMED pesmd のドキュメント "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.4/user-doc/html/pesmd.html> も確認してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:267
msgid ""
"To perform metadynamics, you can review the keywords on: "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html>."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics を実行する際は、<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-"
"doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html> で Keyword を確認できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:269
msgid ""
"To use the adaptive path-CV, you can review the keywords in the header of "
"the file `PathCV.cpp` in the folder `plumed` in the folder for this "
"exercise. To see the html documentation on the path-CV in a browser, open "
"<PMD_exercise/plumed/plumed-2.3.0/user-doc/html/_p_a_t_h_c_v.html> in a "
"browser."
msgstr ""
"Adaptive Path-CV の Keyword は、演習フォルダの `plumed` 内にある `PathCV.cpp` の Header "
"で確認できます。Path-CV の HTML ドキュメントを見るには、<PMD_exercise/plumed/plumed-2.3.0/user-"
"doc/html/_p_a_t_h_c_v.html> を Browser で開いてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:274
msgid ""
"To construct a FES from the metadynamics hills, use the `plumed sum\\_hills`"
" functionality. Consult its features on: "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-doc/html/sum_hills.html>. We "
"recommend to use `--stride` 1 and `--mintozero`."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics の Hill から FES を構築するには、`plumed sum\\_hills` を使います。機能は "
"<https://plumed.github.io/doc-v2.3/user-doc/html/sum_hills.html> "
"を参照してください。`--stride` 1 と `--mintozero` を推奨します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:279
msgid "Exercise 1"
msgstr "演習1"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:281
msgid ""
"The first exercise is found in the folder: "
"`masterclass-22-09/exercises/0_md`."
msgstr "最初の演習は `masterclass-22-09/exercises/0_md` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:283
msgid ""
"This first exercise is meant to get acquainted with running the `plumed "
"pesmd` engine, understanding the input files, and plotting the MD trajectory"
" in the MB potential from the colvar file using gnuplot (or other plotting "
"software). To use the `./run.me` script to start the simulation, first make "
"the script executable using:"
msgstr ""
"この最初の演習では、`plumed pesmd` エンジンの実行、入力ファイルの理解、colvar ファイルから "
"gnuplot（または別の描画ソフトウェア）を使って MB Potential 上の MD Trajectory "
"を描くことに慣れます。`./run.me` でシミュレーションを開始するには、まず次のように実行権限を与えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:293
msgid "Use PLUMED pesmd to run regular MD on the MB PES."
msgstr "PLUMED pesmd で MB PES 上の通常の MD を実行してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:295
msgid "What do you observe?"
msgstr "何が観測されますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:297
msgid ""
"How would you change the behaviour of the system without using an enhanced "
"sampling method (just modifying the MD run parameters)?"
msgstr "Enhanced Sampling 法を使わず、MD の実行パラメータの変更だけで系の挙動を変えるには、どうすればよいでしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:301
msgid "Exercise 2"
msgstr "演習2"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:303
msgid ""
"This exercise is found in the folder: "
"`masterclass-22-09/exercises/1_metadynamics`."
msgstr "この演習は `masterclass-22-09/exercises/1_metadynamics` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:306
msgid ""
"Before you can run the metadynamics simulation, the `plumed.dat` should be "
"completed:"
msgstr "Metadynamics を実行する前に `plumed.dat` を完成させてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:323
msgid "Use PLUMED pesmd to run metadynamics on the MB PES."
msgstr "PLUMED pesmd で MB PES 上の Metadynamics を実行してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:325
msgid "Here are some hints for defining the `METAD` rule:"
msgstr "`METAD` の定義に関するヒントを示します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:326
msgid ""
"the CVs are here the `DISTANCE` components `cv.x` and `cv.y`, which are "
"actually the coordinates of a \"2D particle\" (with respect to the origin) "
"undergoing a Langevin dynamics on the MB PES. Use these components as the "
"`ARG` arguments in the `METAD` rule."
msgstr ""
"ここでの CV は `DISTANCE` の成分 `cv.x` と `cv.y` で、MB PES 上で Langevin Dynamics "
"に従う「2次元粒子」の原点に対する座標です。これらの成分を `METAD` の `ARG` 引数に指定します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:330
msgid "reasonable widths of the Gaussians (`SIGMA`) are ca. 0.1."
msgstr "Gaussian の幅 (`SIGMA`) は約0.1が妥当です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:331
msgid "0.1 is also a reasonable Gaussian height"
msgstr "Gaussian の高さも0.1が妥当です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:332
msgid "a good interval for depositing Gaussians is probably around 500"
msgstr "Gaussian の追加間隔は、おそらく500程度が適切です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:333
msgid ""
"don't forget to define an output `FILE`, that can afterward be read using "
"`plumed sum_hills` to generate and plot the free energy landscape."
msgstr ""
"出力 `FILE` の指定を忘れないでください。後で `plumed sum_hills` で読み込み、自由エネルギー地形を生成・描画できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:337
msgid "Try to obtain a good FES reflecting the two minima."
msgstr "2つの極小を反映する良好な FES を得てください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:339
msgid ""
"Vary the width of the Gaussians for each CV in a systematic manner, what "
"effect do you observe?"
msgstr "各 CV の Gaussian の幅を系統的に変えると、どのような影響が見られますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:342
msgid ""
"Vary the height and deposition frequency of the Gaussians, what trends do "
"you observe?"
msgstr "Gaussian の高さと追加頻度を変えると、どのような傾向が見られますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:345
msgid ""
"How many crossings and recrossings do you sample in a single run for each "
"choice of parameters?"
msgstr "各パラメータ設定について、1回の実行で何回の Crossing と Recrossing が Sampling されますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:349
msgid "Exercise 3"
msgstr "演習3"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:351
msgid ""
"This exercise is found in the folder: "
"`masterclass-22-09/exercises/2_fixedpathmetadynamics`."
msgstr "この演習は `masterclass-22-09/exercises/2_fixedpathmetadynamics` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:354
msgid ""
"Run metadynamics along a fixed path-CV on the MB PES. We recommend using 20 "
"transition nodes, with 20 trailing nodes at each end (60 nodes in total). "
"Use harmonic walls to keep the sampling within a relevant [-0.2,1.2] "
"$\\sigma$-range."
msgstr ""
"MB PES 上の固定 Path-CV に沿って Metadynamics を実行してください。Transition Node は20個、両端の "
"Trailing Node はそれぞれ20個（合計60個）を推奨します。Harmonic Wall を使い、対象の [-0.2,1.2] "
"$\\sigma$ 範囲内に Sampling を維持してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:359
msgid ""
"Now there's only one dimension for the Gaussian width, how do you interpret "
"it?"
msgstr "Gaussian の幅が1次元だけになりました。これをどう解釈しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:362
msgid ""
"Does the diffusion of the system along $\\sigma$ reflect anything "
"particular? What could be the reason?"
msgstr "$\\sigma$ に沿う系の拡散に、何か特徴はありますか？その原因は何でしょうか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:365
msgid "What happens if you add and strengthen a tube potential?"
msgstr "Tube Potential を追加し、強くすると何が起きますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:367
msgid "What is the final path and free energy that you obtain?"
msgstr "最終的にどのような Path と自由エネルギーが得られますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:370
msgid "Exercise 4"
msgstr "演習4"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:372
msgid ""
"This exercise is found in the folder: "
"`masterclass-22-09/exercises/3_adaptivepathmetadynamics`."
msgstr "この演習は `masterclass-22-09/exercises/3_adaptivepathmetadynamics` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:375
msgid ""
"First, change the `plumed.dat` input file to make the path adaptive by "
"changing `PACE`, `STRIDE`, and `HALFLIFE`."
msgstr ""
"まず、`plumed.dat` の `PACE`、`STRIDE`、`HALFLIFE` を変更し、Path を Adaptive にしてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:378
msgid ""
"Run metadynamics along an adaptive path-CV on the MB PES. For "
"simplification, start with the same pace for the metadynamics Gaussians and "
"the path update."
msgstr ""
"MB PES 上の Adaptive Path-CV に沿って Metadynamics を実行してください。簡単のため、最初は "
"Metadynamics の Gaussian と Path 更新の間隔を同じにします。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:382
msgid ""
"For simplification, you can keep only 20 transition nodes, and not use "
"trailing nodes."
msgstr "簡単のため、Transition Node を20個だけにし、Trailing Node は使わなくてもかまいません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:385
msgid ""
"Use harmonic walls to keep the sampling within a relevant [-0.2,1.2] "
"$\\sigma$-range."
msgstr "Harmonic Wall を使い、対象の [-0.2,1.2] $\\sigma$ 範囲内に Sampling を維持してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:388
msgid ""
"What do you expect if you vary the ratio between the metadynamics and the "
"path update frequency?"
msgstr "Metadynamics と Path 更新の頻度の比を変えると、何が起きると予想しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:391
msgid ""
"Vary the tube potential strength and the half-life parameter, what trend do "
"you observe?"
msgstr "Tube Potential の強さと半減期パラメータを変えると、どのような傾向が見られますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:394
msgid ""
"A small value for the `HALFLIFE` (say 1000 MD steps), keeps the path "
"flexible so that the path evolves efficiently away from a poor initial guess"
" path. However, once it has reached the transition channel, it would be "
"better to set it to a very large value, in order to converge to the average "
"transition path. Run first a short PMD simulation using a flexible path and "
"relatively large Gaussians, until the system has filled both basins and has "
"recrossed back to the initial state. Then, restart the simulation, using "
"smaller Gaussians and a large halflife. Use the `INFILE` directive (instead "
"of `GENPATH`) to read the last updated path, which can be taken from the "
"tail of the path.out file of the first run."
msgstr ""
"`HALFLIFE` を小さく（例えば1000 MD Step に）すると Path が柔軟になり、不適切な初期推定 Path "
"から効率よく離れられます。ただし Transition Channel に到達した後は、Average Transition Path "
"に収束させるため、非常に大きい値にする方がよいでしょう。まず柔軟な Path と比較的大きい Gaussian で短い PMD を実行し、両方の "
"Basin が埋まり、初期状態へ戻るまで続けます。次に、小さい Gaussian と大きい半減期で再開します。最初の実行の path.out "
"末尾から最後に更新された Path を取り出し、`GENPATH` の代わりに `INFILE` で読み込んでください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:407
msgid "Exercise 5"
msgstr "演習5"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:409
msgid ""
"This exercise is found in the folder: "
"`masterclass-22-09/exercises/4_multiplewalkers`."
msgstr "この演習は `masterclass-22-09/exercises/4_multiplewalkers` にあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:412
msgid ""
"In this final exercise, you will run the parallel \"multiple walker\" "
"version of path-metadynamics."
msgstr "最後の演習では、Path-metadynamics の並列版「Multiple Walker」を実行します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:415
msgid ""
"Note that with more walkers building the metadynamics simulation, the total "
"run time can be shorter, and possibly also the Gaussians can be smaller."
msgstr "Metadynamics を構築する Walker が増えると、総実行時間を短くでき、Gaussian も小さくできる可能性があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:419
msgid ""
"Try several configurations of walkers and try to answer the question if "
"there is an optimal number of walkers."
msgstr "Walker の構成をいくつか試し、最適な Walker 数があるかを検討してください。"

